    "title": "Mary Gay Scanlon highlights affordability and economic challenges in recent social media posts - South Delco News",
    "text": "Congresswoman Mary Gay Scanlon, who represents Pennsylvania’s 5th district in the U.S. Congress, addressed concerns about economic issues in a series of posts on December 10, 2025.\nIn her first post at 21:39 UTC, Scanlon stated, “I don’t need a chart to tell you:\nGroceries cost too much\nUnemployment is too high\nAffordability isn’t a ‘hoax'”\nShortly after, at 21:40 UTC, she shared two links without additional commentary: “https://t.co/RLdU2zhDXX https://t.co/zT2JaJIHoE”\nLater that evening at 22:07 UTC, Scanlon responded to another user with criticism regarding trade policy and its impact on prices. She wrote, “Really?\nBecause you’ve been here long enough to start a gazillion trade wars that have driven prices way up.”\nMary Gay Scanlon has served as the representative for Pennsylvania’s 5th District since replacing Pat Meehan in 2018. Born in Watertown, New York in 1959 and currently residing in Swarthmore, she holds degrees from Colgate University and the University of Pennsylvania.",
